Grammar

Rule 0     S' -> Program
Rule 1     Program -> ID ID ( ) { Declarations Statements }
Rule 2     Declarations -> Declarations Declaration
Rule 3     Declarations -> Declaration
Rule 4     Declaration -> ID ID ;
Rule 5     Statements -> Statements Statement
Rule 6     Statements -> Statement
Rule 7     Statement -> Assignment
Rule 8     Assignment -> ID = Expression ;
Rule 9     Expression -> Expression + Term
Rule 10    Expression -> Term
Rule 11    Term -> Term * Factor
Rule 12    Term -> Factor
Rule 13    Factor -> INTLIT
Rule 14    Factor -> ID
Rule 15    Factor -> ( Expression )

Terminals, with rules where they appear

(                    : 1 15
)                    : 1 15
*                    : 11
+                    : 9
;                    : 4 8
=                    : 8
ID                   : 1 1 4 4 8 14
INTLIT               : 13
error                : 
{                    : 1
}                    : 1

Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

Assignment           : 7
Declaration          : 2 3
Declarations         : 1 2
Expression           : 8 9 15
Factor               : 11 12
Program              : 0
Statement            : 5 6
Statements           : 1 5
Term                 : 9 10 11

